    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186096674,
      "id": "7294399b-b139-5ee6-824c-5e28e4fc49ff",
      "title": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Already in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cf7ddf5f-fdce-56a9-abbf-633dd8be66dd",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-z &=52 \\\\ y &=10 \\\\ z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & -1 & 52 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 0 & 55 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-5R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bcceee55-454a-5e2e-ad22-e3d8121c98a7",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
