    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "53e03a47-6bd2-5614-bdd8-2d9117d7bc3c",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y-5z &=-15 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+5R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=2$, $y=2$, and $z=5$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle 2,2,5\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "66e4b4ba-b911-5c88-afc2-64e6c8089b4d",
